# Runtime State and Debugging

This Livebook uses only public inspection APIs. It does not read private Agent
Server state.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define And Start An Agent

```elixir
defmodule DebugGuide.Counter do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "debug_guide_counter"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{count: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0)})
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/debug"

    route "counter.add" do
      action %{amount: amount},
        name: "debug_guide_add",
        schema: Zoi.object(%{amount: Zoi.integer()}),
        context: context do
        {:ok, %{context.agent_state | count: context.agent_state.count + amount}}
      end

      define :add, args: [:amount]
    end
  end
end

{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()

{:ok, counter} =
  Jido.start_agent(
    DebugGuide.Counter,
    id: "debug-counter",
    debug: true,
    debug_max_events: 20
  )
```

## Run A Turn

```elixir
{:ok, committed} = DebugGuide.Counter.add(counter, 2)
committed.state
```

## Read Public Views

```elixir
agent = Jido.AgentServer.agent(counter)
status = Jido.AgentServer.status(counter)
snapshot = Jido.AgentServer.snapshot(counter)
children = Jido.AgentServer.children(counter)

%{
  agent: agent,
  status: status,
  snapshot: snapshot,
  children: children
}
```

The snapshot contains portable Agent data and the commit revision. Status is a
narrow runtime view. Child information is for live ownership and can contain
process-local values.

## Read Recent Events

```elixir
{:ok, events} = Jido.AgentServer.recent_events(counter, limit: 10)
Enum.map(events, &Map.take(&1, [:event, :stage, :status]))
```

The event buffer is bounded and newest-first. It is for diagnosis, not durable
audit history.

## Toggle Debug Mode

```elixir
:ok = Jido.AgentServer.set_debug(counter, false)
:ok = Jido.AgentServer.set_debug(counter, true)
```

Use instance debug controls for shared logging and redaction settings. Keep
full payload logging off unless the data policy permits it.

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(counter)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Continue with [Observe Agent Turns](observe-agent-turns.livemd).
